Subject: [PATCH] audio: Mac ARM FFT arithmetic from the profile

Under a macOS ARM profile, Web Audio FFTs run a portable copy of
RustFFT's NEON code, so an x86 host produces the same results a Mac ARM
machine does. The native x86 planner produces different wave tables from
the same input, which a page can read back from an OfflineAudioContext.
FFT plans are cached per size and mode. Other profiles keep the native
planner.

